{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3451","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3451","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3451\",\"parent_revision\":\"8afdd7a719d7047584d554bf287dbc74c7d97d62\",\"root_revision\":\"0160b4d43ee6defd8e98c05d597a5cfbf133757f1b701780d9c55c7578a9ea6f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA plugin is code, and instructions as prose that sometimes call the tools that code exposes, and both feed a harness whose hooks, models and tool-calling semantics are also known. A defect can originate at any of those layers. Nothing in the backlog item schema records which layer is which, so the layer where a symptom was *noticed* becomes the layer where the fix is written.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Repo owner, session melodic-plotting-emerson, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## The Required Behaviour\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nEvery plugin defect starts with one five-row table:\\n\\n1. layer observed\\n2. layer that produced the artifact\\n3. layer that caused it\\n4. layer the fix targets\\n5. layer that will enforce the rule afterwards\\n\\nIn this repo that belongs in the backlog item schema as a field the groom gate validates in code, alongside the label fields whose compliance came out at zero.\\n\\nRow 5 carries a sub-question: **which callers traverse that layer?** A fix placed in prose covers only the callers that read the prose.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nEvery plugin defect starts with one five-row table:\\n\\n1. layer observed\\n2. layer that produced the artifact\\n3. layer that caused it\\n4. layer the fix targets\\n5. layer that will enforce the rule afterwards\\n\\nIn this repo that belongs in the backlog item schema as a field the groom gate validates in code, alongside the label fields whose compliance came out at zero.\\n\\nRow 5 carries a sub-question: **which callers traverse that layer?** A fix placed in prose covers only the callers that read the prose.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why A Validated Field And Not A Documented Convention\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n`scope.md` names two labels \u2014 `**Hypothesis**:` and `**User-provided context**:`. Measured across the 21 items filed in one session: `**Hypothesis**` appeared in **0 of 21**, and 15 of 21 wrote the other label unbolded. A rule stated in prose with no enforcement at any layer produced zero compliance. A validator that refuses the item is the enforcement layer this rule currently lacks.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n`scope.md` names two labels \u2014 `**Hypothesis**:` and `**User-provided context**:`. Measured across the 21 items filed in one session: `**Hypothesis**` appeared in **0 of 21**, and 15 of 21 wrote the other label unbolded. A rule stated in prose with no enforcement at any layer produced zero compliance. A validator that refuses the item is the enforcement layer this rule currently lacks.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed Failures This Convention Would Have Surfaced\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nThree misdiagnoses in one session, each fixing at the layer where the symptom appeared:\\n\\n| Symptom observed | Layer worked | Layer it belonged to |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Duplicate check returned unrelated matches | term-selection code | prose instruction, and a code check that should not block |\\n| SubagentStop hook wrote another agent's task state | the hook's key lookup | the harness fact that transcripts are per-agent, and the prose step that registers at all |\\n| A prose label absent from every item | each item individually | a rule with no enforcement layer |\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nThree misdiagnoses in one session, each fixing at the layer where the symptom appeared:\\n\\n| Symptom observed | Layer worked | Layer it belonged to |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Duplicate check returned unrelated matches | term-selection code | prose instruction, and a code check that should not block |\\n| SubagentStop hook wrote another agent's task state | the hook's key lookup | the harness fact that transcripts are per-agent, and the prose step that registers at all |\\n| A prose label absent from every item | each item individually | a rule with no enforcement layer |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Note\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nA validator can enforce that five layers are named. It cannot enforce that the named layer is correct \u2014 the three failures above were made by someone capable of filling in a form. The gain is that a wrong answer becomes reviewable where an absent field is not.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: the repo owner's framing \u2014 \\\"scope.md naming a label got 0 of 21; a validator refusing the item gets 21 of 21\\\", and \\\"a plugin is code and instructions as prose that sometimes use the tools created by that code, and both of them feed a harness that we also understand all parts of with its hooks and models and tool calling.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nA validator can enforce that five layers are named. It cannot enforce that the named layer is correct \u2014 the three failures above were made by someone capable of filling in a form. The gain is that a wrong answer becomes reviewable where an absent field is not.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: the repo owner's framing \u2014 \\\"scope.md naming a label got 0 of 21; a validator refusing the item gets 21 of 21\\\", and \\\"a plugin is code and instructions as prose that sometimes use the tools created by that code, and both of them feed a harness that we also understand all parts of with its hooks and models and tool calling.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n## Open Question For Grooming\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n`scope.md` forbids unlabelled causal claims at creation and assigns cause verification to grooming. A required \\\"layer that caused it\\\" at creation time would compel the speculation that rule bans. Placement at the groom gate resolves it only if the creation-time schema accepts an unknown value.\\n\\nRows 1 and 2 coincide in most defects. A form that is substantially redundant is filled in mechanically, which is the failure mode of a skimmed instruction wearing a schema.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n`scope.md` forbids unlabelled causal claims at creation and assigns cause verification to grooming. A required \\\"layer that caused it\\\" at creation time would compel the speculation that rule bans. Placement at the groom gate resolves it only if the creation-time schema accepts an unknown value.\\n\\nRows 1 and 2 coincide in most defects. A form that is substantially redundant is filled in mechanically, which is the failure mode of a skimmed instruction wearing a schema.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"bbbeebc92ba38ff8c46bd1faa6f77652e58f55e737670fe4d9a4468f48e3568a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUIyPdg\"}"}